12             Using this program:
13         
14               * Figure 7.8 is intended Integrated Summaries involving a large number of studies. In such cases, displaying
14       ! by-study results
15                 becomes unreasonable. Instead, pool studies and report Last, Min and Max Baseline vs. Last, Min and Max
15       ! Post-baseline measures.
16         
17               * See USER PROCESSING AND SETTINGS, below, to configure this program for your environment and data
18               * Program will plot all visits, ordered by AVISITN, with maximum of 20 boxes on a page (default)
19                 + see user option MAX_BOXES_PER_PAGE, below, to change limit of 20 boxes per page
20               * Program separately plots all parameters provided in PARAMCD
21               * Measurements within each PARAMCD and ATPTN determine precision of statistical results
22                 + MEAN gets 1 extra decimal, STD DEV gets 2 extra decimals
23                 + see macro UTIL_VALUE_FORMAT to modify this behavior
24               * If your treatment names are too long for the summary table, abbreviate them
25                 in the input data, and add a footnote that explains your short Tx codes
26                 + This program contains custom code to shorted Tx labels in the PhUSE CS test data
27                 + See "2b) USER SUBSET of data", below
28         
