52         
53             1) REQUIRED - PhUSE CS Utilities macro library.
54                These templates require the PhUSE CS macro utilities:
55                  https://github.com/phuse-org/phuse-scripts/tree/master/whitepapers/utilities
56                User must ensure that SAS can find PhUSE CS macros in the SASAUTOS path (see EXECUTE ONE TIME, below)
57         
58             2) OPTIONAL - Subset measurement data, to limit resulting plots to specific
59                  - Parameters
60                  - Analysis Timepoints
61                  - Visits
62         
63             3) REQUIRED - Key user settings (libraries, data sets, variables and box plot options)
64                M_LB:   Libname containing ADaM measurement data, such as ADVS.
65                        WORK by default, since step (2) creates the desired WORK subset.
66                M_DS:   Measuments data set, such as ADVS.
67         
68                T_VAR:  Variable in M_DS with the Treatment Name, such as TRTP, TRTA.
69                TN_VAR: Variable in M_DS with the Treatment Number (display controls order), such as TRTPN, TRTAN.
70                M_VAR:  Variable in M_DS with measurements data, such as AVAL.
71                C_VAR:  Variable in M_DS with change-from-baseline data, such as CHG.
72         
73                LO_VAR: Variable in M_DS with LOWER LIMIT of reference range, such as ANRLO.
74                        Required to highlight values outside reference range (RED DOT in box plot), and reference lines
75                HI_VAR: Variable in M_DS with UPPER LIMIT of reference range, such as ANRHI.
76                        Required to highlight values outside reference range (RED DOT in box plot), and reference lines
77         
78                OPTIONAL P-Value settings. Leave this REFERENCE TREATMENT blank to omit p-value from right-hand table.
79                  B_VAR:  Variable in M_DS with baseline measurements, such as BASE.
80                  REF_TRTN: Numeric value of TN_VAR for reference (comparator) treatment
81         
82                P_FL:  Population flag variable, such as SAFFL. 'Y' indicates record is in population of interest.
83         
84                ANALYSIS FLAGS: Define all macro vars. At least one must be non-missing.
85                            NB: Each obs can only be flagged for 1 analysis: Last, Min or Max. CS: Why can't an obs be last AND
85       ! min (or max)? If it is both...
86                  A_LASTFL: Variable flagging LAST post-baseline measures. 'Y' identifies subject values for LAST baseline, LAST
86       ! post-baseline, and CHANGE.
87                  A_MINFL:  Variable flagging MIN  post-baseline measures. 'Y' identifies subject values for MIN  baseline, MIN
87       ! post-baseline, and CHANGE.
88                  A_MAXFL:  Variable flagging MAX  post-baseline measures. 'Y' identifies subject values for MAX  baseline, MAX
88       ! post-baseline, and CHANGE.
89         
90                REF_LINES:
91                      Option to specify which Normal Range reference lines to include in box plots
92                      <NONE | UNIFORM | NARROW | ALL | numeric-value(s)> See discussion in Central Tendency White Paper
93                      NONE    - No reference lines on box plot
94                      UNIFORM - Preferred alternative to default. Only plot LOW/HIGH ref lines if they are uniform for all
94       ! measurements
95                      NARROW  - Default. Display only the narrow normal limits: max LOW, and min HIGH limits
96                      ALL     - Discouraged, since displaying ALL reference lines confuses review of data display
97                      numeric-values - space-delimited list of reference line values, such as a 0 reference line for displays of
97       ! change.
98         
99                MAX_BOXES_PER_PAGE:
100                     Maximum number of boxes to display per plot page (see "Notes", above)
101        
102               OUTPUTS_FOLDER:
103                     Location to write PDF outputs (WITHOUT final back- or forward-slash)
